quran[23]{c,v,t}:
  26,137,This is nothing but the traditions of the ancients.
  26,138,And we will never be punished.’
  26,139,"So they rejected him (i.e. Hud), and We destroyed them. There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them are not believers."
  26,140,"Indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
  26,141,"(The people of) Thamud rejected the messengers,"
  26,142,when their (kinship) brother Salih said to them: ‘Will you not be God-conscious?
  26,143,"Indeed, I am a trustworthy messenger (sent) to you."
  26,144,So be God-conscious and obey me.
  26,145,I do not ask you for any reward for this (message). My reward lies only with the Lord of all worlds.
  26,146,(Do you think that) you will be left secure (forever) in whatever you have here:
  26,147,"In gardens and springs,"
  26,148,"and farms and date palms, having stalks laden with ripe fruits?"
  26,149,And you skillfully hew houses in the mountains.
  26,150,So be God-conscious and obey me.
  26,151,"And do not obey the dictates of the extravagant,"
  26,152,who cause corruption in the land and do not set matters aright.’
  26,153,"They said: ‘Indeed, you are one of the bewitched."
  26,154,You are just a human being like us. So bring us some sign if you are among the truthful.’
  26,155,"He (Salih) said: ‘This is a she-camel. She shall have her turn to drink (water), and you shall have your turn to drink on known days."
  26,156,"And do not touch her with evil intention, lest the punishment of a terrible day overtakes you.’"
  26,157,"But they hamstrung her, and then they became regretful (of killing her)."
  26,158,"So the punishment overtook them. There is indeed a sign in that, but most of them are not believers."
  26,159,"Indeed, your Lord is the All-Mighty, the All-Merciful."
